{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And I will forsake them, etc. And I will hide My face, etc.</b> The intention is that if HaShem were to give His mind to know the troubles that shall come upon them, His mercies would stir and He would remove His wrath. Therefore He announces that He will hide His face, and through this many troubles will find them." "<b>And he will say on that day, etc.</b> Meaning, that they will reckon in their minds, because of the greatness of the trouble they see, that this is only on account of the hiding of My face from them. And this is what He says ״הֲלֹא״ — meaning, surely it is because my Elohim is not within me that they found me, etc.; for if He were within me, not so many troubles would come upon us. And go forth and learn that the prophet said (Judges 10:16): ״וַתִּקְצַר נַפְשׁוֹ בַּעֲמַל יִשְׂרָאֵל״, as it were."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:20:52.932019991Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}